## Context

Upstream published v1.15.0 at `037bba8` on 2026-09-07. The release notes
name PR #55 (uninstall documentation) and PR #57 (durable pause), but the
actual range from the reviewed v1.14.0-era tip `34d6c26` also contains PR #58
(citation style/locale forwarding) and PR #59 (local embedding worker and
optional file logging). A release-note-only update would therefore leave the
review baseline false.

## Work

- pin `UPSTREAM` to the release commit and keep schema generation 2;
- read every changed watched source file, but reconsider only requirement rows whose
  mechanisms changed;
- move stale source citations in `SPEC.md`;
- record the release in `SYNC.md`, `STATE.md`, the deliverables page and a new
  evidence report;
- run the focused upstream tests for pause, worker embedding, logging and the
  adjacent citation change, plus this repository's baseline/schema gates;
- do not carry v1.14 measurements through a changed executable path and do not
  manufacture a live acceptance result where the current adapter is unfaithful.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `UPSTREAM` names current `main` at `5a81cee`, containing v1.15.0, dated
      2026-09-07 and schema 2
- [x] `verification/UPSTREAM-1.15.0-REREAD.md` accounts for the full delta and
      each affected requirement row
- [x] stale source citations are corrected
- [x] focused upstream tests and local baseline/schema gates pass
- [x] relevant trackers record the changed premise
- [x] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass

## Boundaries

No live-library mutation, no upstream post, and no claim that the incomplete
R22/R15 acceptance adapters have measured v1.15.0. This ticket moves the
reviewed source baseline; it does not close trackers 0613, 0648 or 0665.
